# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rules 39 + 40 — FATAL. A secret pushed once is exposed permanently: deleting
# it in a later commit does not remove it from git history. If anything below
# ever reaches a commit, revoke and regenerate the credential immediately.
#
# Save this file as `.gitignore` at the repo root, and commit it BEFORE the
# first commit that could contain a secret.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OAuth 2.0 / Gmail API credentials (Appendix A)
credentials.json
token.json
client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
*token*.json

# Environment and secret files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets.json
*.pem
*.key

# Private per-peer config (config/game.toml, Appendix B p.130-132) IS
# committed here, deliberately — todoFullFix.md §B5's decision: it's a dev
# fixture (same precedent as config/shared/config_dev_g01.json), holds no
# real secrets by design (LLM API keys come from the environment, never from
# this file — Table 21's own framing). Table 20's four *graded* attached
# files don't include it (it never crosses the network, never signed), but
# nothing forbids committing it either, and a fresh clone needs it present
# for the test suite/local dev workflow to work without a bootstrap step.
# Before a REAL match, hand-edit [network].opponent_url and [game] to the
# real values for that match; if a local copy ever needs to differ from what
# should be shared (e.g. a throwaway experiment), use *.local.toml instead:
config/*.local.toml

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Tooling
.ngrok/
ngrok.yml
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*Zone.Identifier*

# PRD 13: bulk, per-run ML pipeline artifacts (training/runs/<run_id>/) —
# not secrets, just build-artifact-shaped noise that would otherwise bloat
# history on every pipeline run. training/promoted/ (the one gated,
# committed checkpoint) is deliberately NOT covered by this — see its own
# note in PRD-13-ml-pipeline-and-deployment.md.
training/runs/

# Course-supplied reference material — copyrighted (all rights reserved),
# not required by any rule to be *in* the repo, and not ours to redistribute.
# Keep them on disk for local reference; never commit them.
police_thief_p2p.pdf
software_submission_guidelines-V3.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored — these are graded artifacts:
#   config/shared/   negotiated configs, one per game (mandatory rule 4)
#   logs/            match logs needed for replay and audit (rule 20)
#   docs/            belief-map and "Verified OK" screenshots (rule 42)
#   PRD/ PLAN.md TODO.md                                       (rule 50)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
